{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BLLTFVn1AWf3bcVwbWCSyZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SOS Card Implementation — Glossary\n2\t\n3\tThe shared vocabulary for implementing the ten SOS cards in this workspace.\n4\tThis file is a **glossary only** — it defines what each term *is*, not how to\n5\tbuild it. The build plan, engine symbols, and per-card guidance live in\n6\t`TODO.md`. When `card_spec.json` oracle text uses one of these words, this is\n7\twhat it means; confirm timing and edge cases against `RULEBOOK.txt`.\n8\t\n9\t## Keyword mechanics on the target cards\n10\t\n11\t**Converge**\n12\tA spell whose effect scales on *X = the number of different colors of mana\n13\tspent to cast it* (not its mana value). Appears on sos_4.\n14\t\n15\t**Affinity for creatures**\n16\tA cost reduction: the spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature its\n17\tcontroller controls. Reduces generic mana only, never colored pips. On sos_245\n18\t(and, granted by sos_245, on its controller's instant/sorcery spells).\n19\t\n20\t**Miracle**\n21\tAn alternative cast opportunity: the first card a player draws in a turn may be\n22\tcast for its miracle cost instead of its normal cost, immediately upon being\n23\tdrawn. On sos_201 it is *granted* to instant/sorcery cards in the controller's\n24\thand.\n25\t\n26\t**Casualty N**\n27\tAs a spell is cast, its controller may sacrifice a creature with power N or\n28\tgreater; when they do, the spell is copied and the controller may choose new\n29\ttargets for the copy. On sos_226 it is granted (Casualty 1) to the controller's\n30\tinstant/sorcery spells.\n31\t\n32\t**Prepared** *(SOS-specific)*\n33\tA state a creature can be in. While a creature is prepared, its controller may\n34\tcast a copy of that creature's associated spell; doing so makes it un-prepared.\n35\tOn sos_13.\n36\t\n37\t**Paradigm** *(SOS-specific)*\n38\tAfter a spell with Paradigm first resolves, it is exiled, and at the beginning\n39\tof each of the controller's *first* main phases thereafter they may cast a copy\n40\tof it from exile without paying its mana cost. On sos_120.\n41\t\n42\t**Surveil N**\n43\tLook at the top N cards of your library, then put any number of them into your\n44\tgraveyard and the rest back on top in any order. On sos_97 (the +1 ability).\n45\t\n46\t## Implementation terms\n47\t\n48\t**SOS card**\n49\tA card in the SOS set, implemented in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. The ten\n50\tto build here are 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257.\n51\t\n52\t**FDN reference card / analogue**\n53\tA completed, correct card in `cards/fdn/`. The reference library: the nearest\n54\tFDN card that already does a mechanic is the example to mirror.\n55\t\n56\t**Spec**\n57\t`card_spec.json` — name, mana cost, type line, and `oracle_text`. Together with\n58\t`RULEBOOK.txt`, the spec is the **source of truth** for a card's behavior. Not\n59\tyour own tests, and not this plan.\n60\t\n61\t**Shared seam**\n62\tAn existing engine extension point (a card hook, a registry, or a helper\n63\tfunction) that more than one target card reuses. Building or learning a seam\n64\tonce and reusing it is the goal.\n65\t\n66\t**Engine gap**\n67\tA mechanic no existing seam covers. Each gap on these ten cards is needed by\n68\texactly one card; a gap is filled with the smallest card-local change, never a\n69\tgeneral subsystem.\n70\t\n71\t**Cost reduction**\n72\tLowering the generic-mana portion of a spell's cost by some count. The engine\n73\tclamps it at zero and never reduces colored pips.\n74\t\n75\t**Free cast**\n76\tPutting a card onto the stack and resolving it without paying its mana cost,\n77\toften from a zone other than hand (graveyard, exile).\n78\t\n79\t**Spell copy**\n80\tA copy of a spell placed on the stack; it resolves on its own and never moves\n81\tbetween zones. New targets may be chosen for the copy.\n82\t\n83\t**Additive-only engine rule**\n84\tThe engine may be extended (new methods, classes, helpers, files) and existing\n85\tfunction bodies may be edited, but nothing existing may be renamed, moved, or\n86\tdeleted. Other modules import engine symbols by name, so a rename or move breaks\n87\tthose imports.\n88\t\n89\t**Card location invariant**\n90\tEach card's class must remain importable from its own\n91\t`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Card directories are never moved or renamed.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"d2b8d64d-9c97-4dc5-a062-189b34e3eed0","timestamp":"2026-06-11T06:47:55.605Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/CONTEXT.md","content":"# SOS Card Implementation — Glossary\n\nThe shared vocabulary for implementing the ten SOS cards in this workspace.\nThis file is a **glossary only** — it defines what each term *is*, not how to\nbuild it. The build plan, engine symbols, and per-card guidance live in\n`TODO.md`. When `card_spec.json` oracle text uses one of these words, this is\nwhat it means; confirm timing and edge cases against `RULEBOOK.txt`.\n\n## Keyword mechanics on the target cards\n\n**Converge**\nA spell whose effect scales on *X = the number of different colors of mana\nspent to cast it* (not its mana value). Appears on sos_4.\n\n**Affinity for creatures**\nA cost reduction: the spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature its\ncontroller controls. Reduces generic mana only, never colored pips. On sos_245\n(and, granted by sos_245, on its controller's instant/sorcery spells).\n\n**Miracle**\nAn alternative cast opportunity: the first card a player draws in a turn may be\ncast for its miracle cost instead of its normal cost, immediately upon being\ndrawn. On sos_201 it is *granted* to instant/sorcery cards in the controller's\nhand.\n\n**Casualty N**\nAs a spell is cast, its controller may sacrifice a creature with power N or\ngreater; when they do, the spell is copied and the controller may choose new\ntargets for the copy. On sos_226 it is granted (Casualty 1) to the controller's\ninstant/sorcery spells.\n\n**Prepared** *(SOS-specific)*\nA state a creature can be in. While a creature is prepared, its controller may\ncast a copy of that creature's associated spell; doing so makes it un-prepared.\nOn sos_13.\n\n**Paradigm** *(SOS-specific)*\nAfter a spell with Paradigm first resolves, it is exiled, and at the beginning\nof each of the controller's *first* main phases thereafter they may cast a copy\nof it from exile without paying its mana cost. On sos_120.\n\n**Surveil N**\nLook at the top N cards of your library, then put any number of them into your\ngraveyard and the rest back on top in any order. On sos_97 (the +1 ability).\n\n## Implementation terms\n\n**SOS card**\nA card in the SOS set, implemented in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. The ten\nto build here are 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257.\n\n**FDN reference card / analogue**\nA completed, correct card in `cards/fdn/`. The reference library: the nearest\nFDN card that already does a mechanic is the example to mirror.\n\n**Spec**\n`card_spec.json` — name, mana cost, type line, and `oracle_text`. Together with\n`RULEBOOK.txt`, the spec is the **source of truth** for a card's behavior. Not\nyour own tests, and not this plan.\n\n**Shared seam**\nAn existing engine extension point (a card hook, a registry, or a helper\nfunction) that more than one target card reuses. Building or learning a seam\nonce and reusing it is the goal.\n\n**Engine gap**\nA mechanic no existing seam covers. Each gap on these ten cards is needed by\nexactly one card; a gap is filled with the smallest card-local change, never a\ngeneral subsystem.\n\n**Cost reduction**\nLowering the generic-mana portion of a spell's cost by some count. The engine\nclamps it at zero and never reduces colored pips.\n\n**Free cast**\nPutting a card onto the stack and resolving it without paying its mana cost,\noften from a zone other than hand (graveyard, exile).\n\n**Spell copy**\nA copy of a spell placed on the stack; it resolves on its own and never moves\nbetween zones. New targets may be chosen for the copy.\n\n**Additive-only engine rule**\nThe engine may be extended (new methods, classes, helpers, files) and existing\nfunction bodies may be edited, but nothing existing may be renamed, moved, or\ndeleted. Other modules import engine symbols by name, so a rename or move breaks\nthose imports.\n\n**Card location invariant**\nEach card's class must remain importable from its own\n`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Card directories are never moved or renamed.\n","numLines":92,"startLine":1,"totalLines":92}}}
