{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012CMaLaWYgNoAAVzyYh7p8p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the information I need. Let me start implementing. I'll follow the build order in TODO.md.\n\n## E1 — Fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n\nIn `engine/casting.py`, after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`, add:\n```python\nfrom engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\ngame.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n    game,\n    SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, card=card, controller=player)\n)\n```\n\n## E2 — Add BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\nI need to define the new event class in `engine/events.py`, then fire it in `engine/game_state.py`'s `advance_phase` method right after emptying mana pools when entering the precombat main phase.\n\n## E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction\n\nNow I'm looking at how to collect cost reductions from permanents on the battlefield. I need to check if a spell is an instant or sorcery, then iterate through all permanents to see if any of them provide spell cost reduction, aggregating those values together.\n\nI'll start with the first example. Together as One is a sorcery with a converge mechanic — it lets a target player draw X cards, deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast it. The Dawning Archaic is a legendary creature that costs one less for each instant and sorcery in your graveyard and has reach. Witherbloom has affinity for creatures on both itself and your instant and sorcery spells, reducing costs by one for each creature you control, plus it flies and has deathtouch. Now looking at Silverquill, the Disputant... So the trigger fires when I cast an instant or sorcery while Silverquill is in play, and I need to prompt the player to choose a creature to sacrifice—if they decline or the creature doesn't have power 1 or greater, nothing happens, but if valid, I sacrifice it and copy the spell onto the stack with new target options. Now I'm moving on to implement Great Hall of the Biblioplex. Writing card definitions... The oracle text references casting a copy of the spell while prepared, which refers to the back face Swords to Plowshares. I need to implement a helper class that exiles a target creature and gives its controller life equal to its power. Now looking at the next card, Lorehold the Historian...\n\nAdding card definitions...\n\nNow I'm ready to implement the systematic changes, starting with the KEY_DECISIONS.md file and then moving through the engine modifications. I should also review how DeterministicPlayer works to understand the player implementation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7110,"cache_read_input_tokens":90183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7110},"output_tokens":34,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"9565810c-6bca-44b5-a0c6-91690de6f7ed","request_id":"req_011Cbw2YhxmrKS6fXU6wYEWT"}
