{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01SVnGEsMEXEZVSJ2tb5c93T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have everything I need. Let me start implementing.\n\nFor targeting in Together as One:\n- `get_targets` needs to return two TargetRequirements\n- Target 1: any player (for draw)\n- Target 2: any player or creature (for damage)\n\nBut looking at how `cast_spell` handles targets:\n```python\ntarget_specs = card.get_targets(game)\nchosen_targets: list[Any] = []\nif target_specs:\n    for spec in target_specs:\n        target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n```\n\nSo it iterates over each spec and calls choose_target once per spec. In `on_resolve`, targets are available via `self.chosen_targets` as a list.\n\nSo for Together as One:\n- chosen_targets[0] = target player (for draw/life)\n- chosen_targets[1] = any target (for damage)\n\nThe oracle text specifies: target player draws, the spell deals damage to any target, and the controller gains life. I need to figure out the zone parameter for TargetRequirement to specify where legal targets come from.\n\nFor player targeting, they're not really in a zone like creatures are. Let me check how existing cards handle this—I'll look at Refute which uses `zone=Zone.STACK`, and then examine other FDN cards that target players to see the pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4503,"cache_read_input_tokens":101171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4503},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"f3eea046-d63e-450f-a889-32af37bd9593","request_id":"req_011Cbw2f6p7byqsTu5tMcG1N"}
