{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BB2s5pw1Sfv3zGYFq9qtyv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have enough understanding now. Let me start implementing everything. This will be a significant amount of code.\n\nLet me plan the implementation structure:\n\n## Phase 1: Engine Changes\n\n### E1: Fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent in cast_spell\n\nIn `engine/casting.py`, after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`:\n```python\nfrom engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\ngame.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n    game,\n    SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, card=card, controller=player)\n)\n```\n\n### E2: Add BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\n\nAdding a new event class for when the precombat main phase begins, then firing it in the phase advancement logic when we transition into that phase.\n\n### E3: Battlefield cost reduction\n\nUpdating the cost reduction logic to account for battlefield effects on instant and sorcery spells.\n\n### Restricted Mana (for sos_257)\n\nAdding a restricted mana pool to track mana that can only be used for specific spell types, with methods to add restricted mana, check if we can pay with it, and consume it. I'll need to add a flag to control whether the restricted pool is included when calculating available mana, then toggle that flag in the casting logic depending on what we're trying to cast.\n\nBefore I start writing the implementations, let me check what's already in `continuous_effects.py` to understand how temporary effects like \"until end of turn\" pumps are handled.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":967,"cache_read_input_tokens":114922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":967},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_i