{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Mq7tySParao73QrJF7qG5Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, I have enough context now. Let me now write all the implementation code systematically.\n\nFor the sos_257 animation pump effect (\"until end of turn\"), I'll use the ContinuousEffect system with DURATION_END_OF_TURN and a P/T modification.\n\nLet me now start writing the code, card by card.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### E1: Fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent\nEdit `casting.py` line ~246 (after game.stack.push(stack_obj))\n\n### E2: BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\n1. Add to `events.py`\n2. Fire in `game_state.py` advance_phase\n\n### E3: Battlefield cost reduction\nEdit `casting.py` get_cost_reduction\n\n### sos_4 - Together as One\nSimple sorcery with two targets, reads colors_spent\n\n### sos_1 - The Dawning Archaic\nCreature with cost_reduction, Reach, attack trigger, exile-instead replacement\n\n### sos_245 - Witherbloom\nCreature with cost_reduction (for itself), spell_cost_reduction (for E3)\n\n### sos_226 - Silverquill\nCreature, register_triggers on SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n\n### sos_257 - Great Hall\nLand, mana abilities with restricted mana and animated creature ability\n\n### sos_57 - Mana Sculpt\nCounterspell with delayed mana via E2\n\n### sos_120 - Improvisation Capstone\nExile from library, cast free, paradigm shift\n\n### sos_13 - Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\nETB token, prepared state, cast Swords copy\n\n### sos_201 - Lorehold, the Historian\nFlying/Haste, Miracle, opponent upkeep loot\n\n### sos_97 - Ral Zarek\nPlaneswalker with surveil, discard, reanimate, coin flip, and turn-skipping abilities\n\nNow I'm ready to start implementing. I'll create KEY_DECISIONS.md first, then work through all the changes. For sos_257's restricted mana, I'm planning to extend ManaPool to handle the new constraints.\n\nAdding restricted mana tracking... Writing ManaPool implementation... I'm realizing the simplest approach is to treat restricted mana as a separate pool that only gets included in payment checks and actual spending when the context allows it—like when casting instant or sorcery spells. The key insight is that when a land produces mana with restrictions, that mana gets tagged with what it can be used for, and I need to track whether it's being spent according to those restrictions.\n\nDefining the ManaPool class... Writing mana pool logic... Finishing the deduction logic...\n\nI'm realizing this approach is getting complicated because I need to track which mana came from which source during payment. A simpler strategy would be to treat restricted mana as a secondary resource that only gets used after the normal pool is exhausted. That way, after payment completes, I can determine what was actually consumed by comparing the remaining balances. Writing payment logic... I need to reconsider the split logic when deducting mana. The key insight is that restricted mana has a specific purpose—it can only be spent on instant or sorcery spells—so when paying for those spells, I should prefer to use unrestricted mana first, preserving the restricted pool for other potential payments within the same priority window. After the payment, if the remaining combined mana is less than the original unrestricted amount, that means all unrestricted mana was consumed and we're drawing from the restricted pool. Writing the mana allocation logic... I'm considering whether the hybrid mana handling in the static method needs adjustment, but since it receives an already-modified remaining dict, it should work as-is. The approach of adding restricted mana directly to the pool is cleaner than creating a separate attribute on the player, so I'll stick with that. Now I need to write out the full implementation and then set up a test to verify that triggers like BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent fire correctly. For E1, I need a probe trigger to confirm that casting an instant fires the event exactly once with the correct controller and spell. For E2, I'll verify the precombat main phase event fires and that any mana added by a trigger persists through the phase transition. For E3, I'll check that a permanent with spell cost reduction on the battlefield actually reduces an instant's generic cost, clamped to zero. These tests should go in the first card's test file. I'll just run the existing engine tests to verify everything works. Now I'm ready to write the implementation—starting with the key decisions document, then the engine modifications, followed by each card with its tests. I'll tackle the most fundamental changes first, beginning with sos_4 which has a 6 generic mana cost where X equals the number of colors spent, allowing the player to draw X cards, deal X damage to any target, and gain X life.\n\nFor sos_201, I need to handle the miracle mechanic where all instant and sorcery cards in hand get miracle {2} while Lorehold is on the battlefield. When a player draws a card as their first draw of the turn, I check if it's an instant or sorcery and if Lorehold is in play, then offer them the option to cast it for {2} instead of the normal cost. The issue is that cast_spell_free bypasses mana payment entirely, but I need the player to actually pay {2}. I could manually deduct {2} from their mana pool first, then use cast_spell_free from hand to put the card on the stack. Let me check how cast_spell_free handles the from_zone parameter to make sure this works correctly. Now I'm thinking through Ral Zarek's abilities and how to handle targeting for loyalty abilities. The engine expects `self.chosen_targets` to be populated by the activation system rather than resolving targets manually, so I need to understand how planeswalker loyalty abilities receive their target information.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1665,"cache_read_input_tokens":115889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1665},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"74224af6-a7a2-41a9-a6d7-504a756ae98e","request_id":"req_011Cbw2puD9LyrbKT4kJEGWq"}
