{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked the `execute-todo` skill to implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace`. The task requires:\n   - Implementing 3 shared engine changes (E1, E2, E3) first\n   - Then implementing 10 SOS cards in dependency order: sos_4, sos_1, sos_245, sos_226, sos_257, sos_57, sos_120, sos_13, sos_201, sos_97\n   - Writing 2-5 tests per card using the real engine via test_utils\n   - Running `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each card\n   - Committing each card individually\n   - Never stopping to ask questions, logging decisions in `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Magic: The Gathering card engine with zones, triggers, replacement effects, casting pipeline\n   - `TriggerRegistration` / `TriggerManager` for triggered abilities\n   - `ReplacementEffect` / `ReplacementManager` for replacement effects\n   - `cast_spell` / `cast_spell_free` for spell casting pipeline\n   - `move_to_zone` for zone transitions with ETB/LTB hooks\n   - `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (E1), `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` (E2) event classes\n   - `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell) -> int` method protocol for E3 battlefield reductions\n   - `ManaPool._restricted_instant_sorcery` and `_instant_sorcery_context` for restricted mana\n   - `DeterministicPlayer._script` deque: `appendleft` adds to front, `popleft` (called by `choose_target`) pops from front - targets must be appended in REVERSE order\n   - `AttacksTriggeredEvent` now fired in `declare_attackers_step` (was never fired before)\n   - `set_board_state` does NOT register triggers; must call `register_triggers(game)` manually\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` - Added `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n         pass\n     ```\n\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` - Three changes:\n     1. E1: Fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`:\n        ```python\n        from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n            game,\n            SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, card=card, controller=player),\n        )\n        ```\n     2. E3: Aggregate battlefield reductions in `get_cost_reduction`:\n        ```python\n        if CardType.INSTANT in card.card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card.card_types:\n            for permanent in game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all():\n                reduction_fn = getattr(permanent, \"spell_cost_reduction\", None)\n                if reduction_fn is not None:\n                    raw += reduction_fn(game, card)\n        ```\n     3. Restricted mana context in `cast_spell`:\n        ```python\n        player.mana_pool._instant_sorcery_context = (\n            CardType.INSTANT in card.card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card.card_types\n        )\n        if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(effective_cost):\n            player.mana_pool._instant_sorcery_context = False\n            # Rollback...\n            raise CastingError(...)\n        player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n        player.mana_pool._instant_sorcery_context = False\n        ```\n\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` - Fire E2 in `advance_phase` after `empty_mana_pools()`:\n     ```python\n     if self.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN:\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\n         self.trigger_manager.fire_event(self, BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent())\n     ```\n\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py` - Restricted mana support:\n     ```python\n     # In __init__:\n     self._restricted_instant_sorcery: dict[ManaType, int] = {mt: 0 for mt in ManaType}\n     self._instant_sorcery_context: bool = False\n\n     def add_restricted(self, mana_type: ManaType, amount: int = 1) -> None:\n         if amount < 0:\n             raise ValueError(f\"Cannot add negative restricted mana: {amount}\")\n         self._restricted_instant_sorcery[mana_type] = (\n             self._restricted_instant_sorcery.get(mana_type, 0) + amount\n         )\n\n     # empty() also clears _restricted_instant_sorcery\n     # can_pay() includes restricted when _instant_sorcery_context=True\n     # pay() merges restricted into working pool, then splits back (deducts unrestricted first)\n     ```\n\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` - Fire AttacksTriggeredEvent in `declare_attackers_step`:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n         game,\n         AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker),\n     )\n     ```\n     This was added AFTER setting `is_attacking = True` and tapping the creature.\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` - Complete Sorcery implementation:\n     ```python\n     class TogetherAsOne(Sorcery):\n         def get_targets(self, game):\n             return [\n                 TargetRequirement(filter_fn=lambda obj: hasattr(obj,\"life\") and hasattr(obj,\"zones\"), description=\"target player\", zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD),\n                 TargetRequirement(filter_fn=lambda obj: hasattr(obj,\"life\") or CardType.CREATURE in getattr(obj,\"card_types\",set()), description=\"any target\", zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD),\n             ]\n         def on_resolve(self, game):\n             colors_spent = getattr(self, \"colors_spent\", [])\n             x = len(set(colors_spent))\n             targets = getattr(self, \"chosen_targets\", [])\n             target_player = targets[0] if len(targets) > 0 else None\n             damage_target = targets[1] if len(targets) > 1 else None\n             # target_player draws X, damage_target takes X damage, controller gains X life\n     ```\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` - 6 tests, all passing\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` - Complete Creature implementation with:\n     - `cost_reduction`: count instants/sorceries in controller's graveyard\n     - `register_triggers`: AttacksTriggeredEvent trigger, prompts choose_card from GY, cast_spell_free from GRAVEYARD, wraps StackObject.on_resolve for exile-instead\n     - `_wrap_exile_instead` helper: wraps on_resolve to move card from GY to exile after resolution\n     ```python\n     def _wrap_exile_instead(game, stack_obj, card, controller):\n         original = stack_obj.on_resolve\n         def _on_resolve_with_exile(g):\n             original(g)\n             owner = getattr(card, \"owner\", controller) or controller\n             gy = g.get_graveyard(owner)\n             if gy.contains(card):\n                 gy.remove(card)\n                 g.get_exile(owner).add(card)\n         stack_obj.on_resolve = _on_resolve_with_exile\n     ```\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` - 9 tests, all passing. Uses `_put_on_battlefield` helper:\n     ```python\n     def _put_on_battlefield(game, player_index, card):\n         p = game.players[player_index]\n         card.owner = p\n         card.controller = p\n         game.players[player_index].zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].add(card)\n         card.register_triggers(game)\n         if hasattr(card, \"register_replacement_effects\"):\n             card.register_replacement_effects(game)\n     ```\n\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` - Complete Creature implementation (written, NOT yet tested):\n     ```python\n     class WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature):\n         def cost_reduction(self, game):\n             return _count_creatures(game, self.controller)\n         \n         def spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell):\n             # Called by E3; reduces controller's instants/sorceries\n             if spell.controller is not self.controller:\n                 return 0\n             return _count_creatures(game, self.controller)\n\n     def _count_creatures(game, controller):\n         if controller is None:\n             return 0\n         return sum(1 for perm in game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all()\n                    if CardType.CREATURE in getattr(perm, \"card_types\", set()))\n     ```\n\n   - `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` - Decision log with 15+ entries covering all ambiguous decisions\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Script ordering bug (sos_4 tests)**: `appendleft` adds to front of deque, so calling `p1._script.appendleft(target1)` then `p1._script.appendleft(target2)` results in `[target2, target1]`. First popleft() returns `target2`. Fixed by appending in reverse order: first append the LAST target, then append the FIRST target. Pattern: to make target1 pop first, target2 pop second: `appendleft(target2)` then `appendleft(target1)`.\n   - **test_x_three_three_colors assertion failed (p1.life==20 not 23)**: Wrong script ordering caused p1 to be the damage target. Fixed with correct script order.\n   - **test_cast_instant_from_graveyard_on_attack / test_exile_instead failed**: `set_board_state` doesn't call `register_triggers`. Fixed by creating `_put_on_battlefield` helper that manually calls `register_triggers(game)`.\n   - **AttacksTriggeredEvent never fired**: Despite being defined in events.py and registered by many FDN cards, the event was never actually fired anywhere in combat.py. Fixed by adding `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(...))` in `declare_attackers_step`.\n   - **Exile-instead via replacement_manager**: `move_to_zone` only applies replacements when `leaving_battlefield` (from Zone.BATTLEFIELD). Spell resolution (stack→graveyard) doesn't trigger replacements. Fixed by wrapping StackObject.on_resolve to check graveyard after resolution and move to exile.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Restricted mana (for sos_257)**: Chose `_instant_sorcery_context` flag approach on ManaPool so can_pay/pay honor restrictions without changing function signatures. `pay()` merges restricted into working pool when context=True, then splits back preferring to consume unrestricted mana first.\n   - **Exile-instead for sos_1**: Since replacement_manager only handles leaving-battlefield events, used wrapper approach on StackObject.on_resolve for card-local exile redirection.\n   - **E2 firing point**: Fires after `empty_mana_pools()` in `advance_phase` so any mana a handler adds survives into the main phase.\n   - **E3 controller scoping**: Only aggregates reductions from permanents whose controller IS the casting player.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - User message 1: \"Run the `execute-todo` skill now to implement the SOS cards. Your task and prepared execution plan are in /workspace/TODO.md and /workspace/CONTEXT.md.\"\n   - The execute-todo skill loaded with detailed instructions including: read orientation files, implement checklist items in order, write 2-5 engine-driven tests per card, run engine_tests after each change, commit one card at a time, log decisions in KEY_DECISIONS.md, never stop to ask questions.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - [ ] Write tests for sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer) and commit\n   - [ ] sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant (Flying, Vigilance, Casualty 1 grant via E1)\n   - [ ] sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land, restricted mana, animation to 2/4 Wizard)\n   - [ ] sos_57 — Mana Sculpt (Counterspell + delayed mana via E2)\n   - [ ] sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone (exile from library, cast free, Paradigm via E2)\n   - [ ] sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares (ETB token, Prepared state)\n   - [ ] sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian (Flying/Haste, Miracle, upkeep loot)\n   - [ ] sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (Planeswalker, Surveil, coin flip, skip turns)\n   - [ ] Mark each item [x] in TODO.md after completion\n 