{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01SwZcNW2LA37bCkmkX5DD8y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So triggers are pushed onto the stack as StackObjects. When a spell is cast:\n1. `cast_spell` pushes the spell onto the stack: `stack = [spell]`\n2. `fire_event(SpellCastTriggeredEvent)` runs and pushes trigger StackObjects: `stack = [spell, trigger]`\n3. `_resolve_top_of_stack` resolves items from the top: first resolves the trigger (which asks about sacrifice/copy), then resolves the spell.\n\nSo the trigger resolves BEFORE the spell. When the trigger effect runs, the spell is still on the stack (below the trigger).\nWhen the trigger's `on_resolve` method executes, it's already been popped from the stack, but the spell remains below it waiting to be resolved. So when I access the stack during the trigger effect, the spell should still be there.\n\nAfter sacrificing the spell and pushing a copy on top, the stack resolves from the top down—first the copy, then the original spell—which matches MTG's stack behavior. The test utility then resolves everything on the stack. The trigger fires during the engine's cast, and then `_resolve_top_of_stack` handles everything afterward. When the trigger resolves, it needs to call `choose_card` to pick a sacrifice target and `choose_yes_no` for new targets, but since these choices are appended with `appendleft` during `cast_spell`, they'll be queued before the trigger actually resolves—so the timing should work out correctly. que is `[A, B, ...]` — so I need to reverse the order when using `appendleft`. The `cast_spell` test utility handles targets this way, and I should do the same for my casualty and targeting choices. The key insight is that `choose_card` for the casualty selection fires first after the trigger resolves, so I need to append it last to the deque so it's at the front when needed. Let me trace through a concrete example: casting an instant with Silverquill on the battlefield and a 1/1 creature available to sacrifice, where I want to sacrifice for the copy but not target anything new.\n\nWriting the test cases...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":55378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"bf57b125-dbb8-4ddf-8de0-4fcda0bf0d23","request_id":"req_011Cbw436RHNQekL16VCPXVc"}
