{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JixAU6JYDhqSucxvYKqEk1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the patterns well. Let me now write sos_257.\n\nKey aspects:\n1. `Land` class\n2. Mana ability 1: `{T}: Add {C}` (colorless)\n3. Mana ability 2: `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend only to cast instant/sorcery.`\n   - This uses `add_restricted` for any-color mana\n   - Player needs to choose a color (or we simplify to colorless restricted)\n   - Wait, the spec says \"any color\" — player chooses which color. \n\nFor the any-color mana, I'll let the player choose the color through the script, and the restricted mana will enforce that it's only spent on instants or sorceries.\n\n4. Activated ability: `{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant/sorcery, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.`\n   - This is an `ActivatedAbility` (not mana ability)\n   - Cost: pay {5} generic mana (5 colorless or any mana)\n   - Effect: add a creature type, set power/toughness, and add a triggered ability that triggers when you cast an instant or sorcery to pump the creature +1/+0 until end of turn.\n\n5. The pump trigger: when you cast instant/sorcery, +1/+0 until EOT\n   - I'm incrementing the power by 1 (similar to how Shivan Dragon works)\n   - The \"until EOT\" part is a limitation in the engine since there's no cleanup mechanism modeled, but I should check if there's actually an end-of-turn cleanup system I'm missing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":79684,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":652},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_us