{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01HcsnQDKcxEA8AyXb8aFbTn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that FDN tests do call `on_resolve` directly and set `chosen_targets` directly. Since there's a precedent in the FDN tests, let me use a similar approach for sos_57 - testing the counter mechanics directly.\n\nBut for the delayed mana trigger (which requires E2), I'll need to advance to the precombat main phase and verify the trigger fires.\n\nLet me write tests:\n1. Properties tests\n2. Counter mechanics (can set `chosen_targets` and call `on_resolve` directly since FDN does it)\n3. Delayed mana trigger (set up wizard, counter a spell, advance to precombat main, verify mana)\n4. No mana without Wizard\n\nFor testing the counter through the real engine, I could cast a spell, then cast Mana Sculpt targeting it and resolve both - but this requires careful timing synchronization since Mana Sculpt can only be cast when there's already a spell on the stack. The test would need to cast the opponent's spell first, then Mana Sculpt targeting it, then resolve them in order.\n\nActually, this is getting complicated. I'll take the simpler approach: directly set the targets and call `on_resolve` like the FDN tests do, then use `advance_to_phase` to handle the end-of-turn trigger part. Let me check what `advance_to_phase` offers in the test utilities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1360,"cache_read_input_tokens":118500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1360},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"8c10643c-0ad3-4417-b42b-95a7b1be5504","request_id":"req_011Cbw4uuVsttvDuiNkFV7TZ"}
