{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Ma6sNXxN1bb5BndMSMDjXL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a complex card. Let me break it down:\n\n1. **Main effect**: Exile cards from the top of the library until total mana value ≥ 4. May cast any number of them for free.\n2. **Paradigm**: After first resolution, exile this spell (instead of putting it in graveyard), then register a recurring trigger on E2 to cast a copy from exile for free at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\n\nKey implementation details:\n- `library.top(n)` to look at library cards\n- `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)` for casting from exile\n- `copy_spell(game, original_so, controller)` for creating Paradigm copies\n\nThe tricky part is tracking \"first resolution\" — this needs to be per card name, not per instance, since any copy counts toward that threshold. I'll use a flag on the game state to track whether this card name has resolved before, so the Paradigm trigger only sets up after the very first time.\n\nFor implementation, I'm going with a simpler per-instance approach for now, acknowledging it's a limitation compared to real MTG where multiple copies would share the same \"first resolution\" state.\n\nOn the library exile side, I need to iterate through the top cards, accumulating mana value until I hit 4 or more, then move those cards to exile. After that, I'm letting the player choose which exiled cards to cast, building a list of legal options and processing each choice.\n\nFor Paradigm, the first time this card resolves, I check the flag and if it hasn't activated yet, I move the card to exile, set the flag, and register a recurring trigger at the beginning of each of the controller's first main phases that lets them cast a copy of this card from exile for free. I need to understand how the casting system handles cards in the exile zone.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,