{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01YBzALpg4C5YjawEznxaMYV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. The `move_to_zone` function looks for the card in the source zone. When the engine tries to do `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` after `on_resolve` returns, it first looks for the card in the STACK zone.\n\nBut wait - the card (Improvisation Capstone) was moved from stack zone to stack during `cast_spell_free`. When `_resolve_spell` runs, the card is in the stack zone. After `on_resolve`, the engine calls `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\nIn my `_apply_paradigm` function, I'm adding the card to the exile zone without removing it from the stack first. So the card ends up in both zones simultaneously. Then when `move_to_zone` tries to move it from stack to graveyard, it finds it there and moves it, leaving the card in both exile and graveyard. I need to properly remove it from the stack zone before adding it to exile.\n\nLooking at how similar effects handle \"exile instead of graveyard,\" I see they wrap the stack object's `on_resolve` method to intercept the card after resolution and redirect it to exile. For Paradigm, I should do the same—let the engine move the card to the graveyard normally, then post-resolution, move it to exile instead. The challenge is that I don't have direct access to the stack object from within `on_resolve`, so I need to find a way to wrap the resolution process from outside. Looking at how `move_to_zone` works, replacement effects only fire when a card leaves the battlefield, but the spell resolution calls it without a `replacement_event` parameter anyway, so that won't help. I could manually move the card to exile in `on_resolve` before the engine tries to move it to the graveyard, or I'd need to override the entire resolution flow entirely.\n\nThe first option seems cleaner: I'll remove the card from the stack zone in `_apply_paradigm` so when `move_to_zone` runs, it can't find the card there and returns early. Then I'll add the card to exile instead.\n\nWriting the implementation...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1260,"cache_read_input_tokens":144375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1260},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"7d9f82b8-1b61-413f-9531-b65445fc864e","request_id":"req_011Cbw5FvtmjyG8x2jrseGmL"}
