{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01KDZ5wdEhtDpTVBbgYD84fY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Three issues:\n\n1. `test_skips_lands_from_casting`: Land not in exile. My library has `big` (top) and `land` (bottom). The exile loop peels from top: takes `big` (MV4), total = 4, meets threshold, stops. So `land` is never exiled. The test expectation is wrong - the land should stay in the library because we stop after hitting MV 4 with `big`.\n\nWait, the library order: I add `land` first, then `big`. Since `zone.add` appends, the internal list is `[land, big]`. \n\n`top(1)` returns the last element, which is `big`. So we take `big` first (MV 4 >= 4 threshold met), stop. Land is NOT exiled. I need to redesign the test so the land gets exiled before we hit the threshold - put `land` on top and a MV4 card below it, so we exile both.\n\nNow I'm running into an issue with phase advancement. After the capstone spell sets the phase to PRECOMBAT_MAIN with no step, the phase stays there when trying to advance to BEGINNING/UNTAP, and the phase sequence lookup is failing.\n\nLooking at the test utilities, `cast_spell` handles phase setup by checking if we're not in a main phase and resetting to PRECOMBAT_MAIN with step=None. I need to trace through whether `_cast_capstone` is properly initializing the game state before the cast happens.\n\nThe real issue is that when I set `game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN`, I'm not also setting `game.step = None`. The game is probably starting with `game.step = Step.UNTAP` from initialization, and `advance_phase` can't find the tuple `(Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Step.UNTAP)` in the valid phase sequence. I need to explicitly clear the step when setting the phase.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2038,"cache_read_input_tokens":153540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_token