{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Ljt6PnYsPpjWZuG5djr9MR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key clauses:\n1. **ETB**: target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling token with flying\n2. **After ETB**: if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes prepared\n3. **Prepared state**: While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell (Swords to Plowshares: exile target creature; its controller gains life equal to its power). Doing so unprepares it.\n\nKey decisions:\n- \"Its spell\" refers to Swords to Plowshares (the back face)\n- The card is a 3/3 Cat Cleric with mana cost {1}{W}{W}\n\nImplementing the card class with the creature stats and mana requirements...\n\nNow I need to handle the prepared mechanic: tracking it with a boolean flag, setting up an ETB trigger that creates a Swords to Plowshares copy in exile, and defining an activated ability that lets you cast that copy and then unprepares the creature.\n\nI'm also creating a separate Instant class for Swords to Plowshares that exiles a target creature and has the controller gain life equal to its power.\n\nFor the activated ability, I need to check if the creature is prepared before allowing activation, then cast the copy for free and flip the prepared flag back to false. Let me look at how `create_token` works to understand the token creation process.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":158918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465},"output_tokens":34,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"59816944-ac7c-4f17-bbaa-ea5bbd381592","request_id":"req_011Cbw5UDFrakJQZUAssPn9F"}
