{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Hr3XCkDymTkMGVctrCSFmn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the system:\n\n1. `fire_event` checks all currently-registered triggers against the event.\n2. Any matching triggers get pushed onto the stack as `StackObject`.\n3. Then `_resolve_top_of_stack(game)` pops from the stack and calls `on_resolve` (which is the trigger effect).\n\nIn `zones.py`:\n```python\nif entering_battlefield:\n    game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent=card, ...))\n    if hasattr(card, \"register_triggers\"):\n        card.register_triggers(game)\n```\n\nSo when a card enters the battlefield, the ETB event fires first against only pre-registered triggers, then the card registers its own triggers afterward. This means a card's ETB trigger won't fire on its own entry through this mechanism—the trigger isn't registered yet when the event fires. But the FDN cards use `_self_etb_condition(self)` which checks if `event.permanent is source`, so they shouldn't match. I need to check how the FDN tests actually work, like with Guarded Heir.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the issue might be in how cards are cast. When a spell resolves, maybe the flow is different for creatures—perhaps `register_triggers` gets called before the ETB event fires, or the casting pipeline handles the zone transition differently than a direct `move_to_zone` call. Let me trace through what happens when a card is cast normally versus when it enters the battlefield.\n\nLooking at the zones code, there's a deliberate design pattern here: the ETB event fires first, then `register_triggers` is called. This means the permanent's own ETB trigger isn't registered yet when the event fires, so it can't retroactively trigger off its own entry—but other already-registered triggers watching for ENTERS_BATTLEFIELD will still fire. This seems intentional.\n\nBut now I'm confused about how the FDN cards' ETB effects actually work if their triggers are only registered after they enter. Let me reconsider what `_self_etb_condition` is checking—it looks for `event.permanent is source`, which would only match when that specific card enters, not when other creatures enter later.\n\nI need to trace through how creatures actually resolve when cast to understand when their ETB triggers get registered and when they fire.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":45347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":652},"output_tokens":36,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"e927981d-16d9-4052-a12c-e38c9b414aa9","request_id":"req_011Cbw5uNfqq8sc5aVBJmN8t"}
