{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01TpEDx6b3sNKMaSmo4LXYs8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key finding! Line 432 in `casting.py`:\n```python\nmove_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)\n```\n\nSo when a creature resolves, the casting module calls `move_to_zone(STACK → BATTLEFIELD)`. That goes through the same zones.py path which:\n1. Fires ETB event (trigger not registered yet → doesn't fire based on _self_etb_condition)\n2. Calls `register_triggers` (registers trigger)\n\nBut then... the trigger still wouldn't fire on the creature's own ETB...\nLet me trace through the actual casting pipeline more carefully. When a creature resolves, the StackObject's on_resolve method runs, which calls the Creature's on_resolve, which then moves it from stack to battlefield. I need to check whether register_triggers happens before or after that move fires the ETB event.\n\nLooking at the move_to_zone logic, it seems like the EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent fires before register_triggers is called, which would mean the trigger never fires on its own entry. But maybe the design intent is different — perhaps the condition `event.permanent is source` is meant to catch future entries if the creature somehow enters the battlefield again from another effect. Let me check if there's a test for this behavior.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1681,"cache_read_input_tokens":45999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1681},"output_tokens":37,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"ea4ebae7-e42b-4bfd-b65d-688c1ca223b8","request_id":"req_011Cbw5wJkFzRpqZbH1PKkFA"}
