{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_019HStP3hQAzsJJcLwk7uR3U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full picture:\n\n1. For creatures: when they're cast, the casting pipeline calls `card.on_resolve(game)` BEFORE `move_to_zone(STACK → BATTLEFIELD)`.\n2. In `move_to_zone(STACK → BATTLEFIELD)`: ETB event fires, THEN `register_triggers` is called.\n3. So the ETB trigger is registered AFTER the ETB event fires → the trigger DOESN'T fire on the card's own entry.\n\nBut wait... so how does Guarded Heir create tokens? Let me re-read its `_effect` in `register_triggers`:\nThe effect creates two Knight tokens under the controller's control. But here's the issue: the trigger is registered after the ETB event already fired, so this effect would only trigger when *another* creature enters the battlefield, not when Guarded Heir itself enters. Unless there's a `_self_etb_condition` that changes this behavior...\n\nActually, let me reconsider the order of operations in the zones code. The ETB event fires before the card's own triggers are registered, which means other already-registered triggers can still respond to it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1805,"cache_read_input_tokens":52805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1805},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"157d49f8-c113-401b-88cf-f7ad26aa1c93","request_id":"req_011Cbw61L1XMGm24Jrj8vN7o"}
