{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01MBeiJ2D8XUvCR5RLk8fYqK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, `choose` pops from `_script`. The script uses `deque.popleft()` for FIFO access. When we do `p1._script.appendleft(p2)`, it adds to the LEFT side of the deque. Then `popleft()` returns from the LEFT. So `appendleft(p2)` then `popleft()` → returns p2. Good.\n\nNow my plan:\n\nThe ETB trigger approach doesn't work because the engine fires ETB BEFORE registering triggers. The cleanest solution is to directly push the effect onto the stack from within `register_triggers`. \n\nSince `register_triggers` runs after the card enters the battlefield, the effect executes with the correct game state. I'm modifying `card_impl.py` to push the effect directly onto the stack instead of using a trigger, since the card is already on the battlefield at that point.\n\nWriting the effect handler... After the card moves to the battlefield, `register_triggers` gets called and pushes our StackObject onto the stack, then control returns. I need to figure out whether `_resolve_top_of_stack` is just a test helper or if it's part of the actual casting pipeline that needs to pop and resolve the stack.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":61187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"8e058c8c-ed76-43c9-8f74-3c28c86ab8ef","request_id":"req_011Cbw69rBDDRzi4bztweJEP"}
