{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0137JitrSdrfrUa4ngXcBQEF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `cards_drawn_this_turn` counter is never reset between turns! This is a problem for the miracle mechanic which requires knowing if a card draw is the \"first draw this turn.\" However, the `draw_card` function creates this attribute lazily with `if not hasattr(player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\"): player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0`. So on first draw it's 0, then incremented to 1.\n\nBut there's no reset at the beginning of a new turn. Looking at the untap step, it resets `land_plays_remaining` but not `cards_drawn_this_turn`.\nI could fix this by tracking the turn number when the first draw happens, then checking in the miracle trigger condition whether we're still on that same turn. This way I can determine if a draw is the first one of the current turn without needing to explicitly reset the counter. I could track the first draw of each turn myself using the turn number, but the cleaner approach is to reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` at the start of each turn in the untap step. That way any card mechanic relying on this counter works correctly. Though I'm seeing a note about keeping engine gaps card-local with deliberate limitations instead of fixing them globally. I see the issue now—the condition should only trigger when it's both the first draw of the turn AND the card is an instant or sorcery. If the first draw is a land, miracle shouldn't activate, and if a later draw is an instant, it's too late. The problem with tracking draws is that without resetting the counter each turn, it only works once in the entire game. The cleanest solution is to reset the draw counter during the untap step as an engine-level fix, which keeps things additive and correct. I'm realizing the reset timing matters for how \"this turn\" is interpreted. When the active player's untap step happens, their counter resets to zero. Then during their draw step, they draw a card and the counter increments. But if someone draws a card during an opponent's turn through an effect like looting, that still counts as a draw that happened \"this turn\" in MTG rules, even though it's not the active player's turn. So I need to think through whether the reset should only apply to the active player or if there's a broader interpretation of what \"this turn\" means for effects like miracle.\n\nThe simplest approach is to track draws per player per turn number rather than relying on the untap step reset. I'm setting up a dictionary to store which turn number each player last triggered their miracle condition, so I can check if this is truly the first draw of the current turn. I'm realizing the logic needs to be flipped—I should track whether any card has been drawn this turn, and only trigger miracle if the very first draw is an instant or sorcery. If a non-instant/sorcery gets drawn first, miracle can't fire for the rest of that turn. Let me restructure this to track the first draw event properly and check the card type against that condition. Storing the card reference and returning whether it's an instant or sorcery, then I'll verify the logic handles multiple draws correctly across turn boundaries before moving on to implement the full sos_201 function.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":83815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"484d838e-99f0-4b93-a6df-7ef02938954a","request_id":"req_011Cbw6QgXh6YfWM85gGrhWB"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0137JitrSdrfrUa4ngXcBQEF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good, I have all the patterns I need. Now let me implement sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian):"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":83815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"ff5d06b2-9719-49d1-bb1e-6eb444db8ca3","request_id":"req_011Cbw6QgXh6YfWM85gGrhWB"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0137JitrSdrfrUa4ngXcBQEF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RgcgksCfYmTdXP4AmU4rEN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py","content":"\"\"\"Card implementation for Lorehold, the Historian.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n\nfrom engine.card import Creature\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Supertype, Zone\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n\n\nclass LoreholdsTheHistorian(Creature):\n    \"\"\"Lorehold, the Historian — {3}{R}{W} — 5/5 Legendary Elder Dragon.\n\n    Flying, haste.\n    Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\n    At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card.\n    If you do, draw a card.\n\n    SOS collector number 201.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Lorehold, the Historian\")\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{3}{R}{W}\"))\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"})\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"supertypes\", {Supertype.LEGENDARY})\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"keywords\", Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 5)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 5)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\n            \"rules_text\",\n            \"Flying, haste\\n\"\n            \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may \"\n            \"cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card \"\n            \"you drew this turn.)\\n\"\n            \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. \"\n            \"If you do, draw a card.\",\n        )\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n\n    def register_triggers(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n        \"\"\"Register miracle draw trigger and opponent-upkeep loot trigger.\"\"\"\n        from engine.casting import CastingError, cast_spell_free\n        from engine.events import BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent, DrawsCardTriggeredEvent\n        from engine.game import discard, draw_card\n        from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n\n        source = self\n        controller = getattr(self, \"controller\", None) or game.active_player\n\n        # --- Miracle {2} trigger ---\n        # Track the first draw per (player, turn_number) so we can detect the\n        # first draw of each turn without an engine-level counter reset.\n        _first_draw_turn: dict[int, int] = {}\n        _miracle_queue: deque = deque()\n\n        def _miracle_condition(game: Any, event: Any) -> bool:\n            ctrl = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n            if ctrl is None or event.player is not ctrl:\n                return False\n            current_turn = game.turn_number\n            player_id = id(ctrl)\n            if _first_draw_turn.get(player_id) == current_turn:\n                return False  # Not the first draw this turn\n            # Mark this turn's first draw (regardless of card type)\n            _first_draw_turn[player_id] = current_turn\n            card = event.card\n            if card is None:\n                return False\n            card_types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n            is_inst_sorc = CardType.INSTANT in card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card_types\n            if is_inst_sorc:\n                _miracle_queue.append(card)\n            return is_inst_sorc\n\n        def _miracle_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n            ctrl = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n            if ctrl is None or not _miracle_queue:\n                return\n            card = _miracle_queue.popleft()\n            if not game.get_hand(ctrl).contains(card):\n                return\n            try:\n                cast_it = ctrl.choose_yes_no(f\"Cast {card.name} for miracle {{2}}?\")\n            except Exception:\n                cast_it = False\n            if not cast_it:\n                return\n            try:\n                cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, card, Zone.HAND)\n            except CastingError:\n                pass\n\n        game.trigger_manager.register(\n            TriggerRegistration(\n                event_type=DrawsCardTriggeredEvent,\n                condition=_miracle_condition,\n                effect=_miracle_effect,\n                source=source,\n                controller=controller,\n            )\n        )\n\n        # --- Opponent's upkeep loot trigger ---\n        def _upkeep_condition(game: Any, event: Any) -> bool:\n            ctrl = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n            if ctrl is None:\n                return False\n            return game.active_player is not ctrl\n\n        def _upkeep_effect(game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n            ctrl = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n            if ctrl is None:\n                return\n            hand = game.get_hand(ctrl)\n            hand_cards = hand.get_all()\n            if not hand_cards:\n                return\n            try:\n                discard_it = ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Discard a card to draw a card?\")\n            except Exception:\n                discard_it = False\n            if not discard_it:\n                return\n            try:\n                to_discard = ctrl.choose_card(hand_cards, \"choose card to discard\")\n            except Exception:\n                to_discard = hand_cards[-1]\n            if to_discard is not None and hand.contains(to_discard):\n                discard(game, ctrl, to_discard)\n                draw_card(game, ctrl)\n\n        game.trigger_manager.register(\n            TriggerRegistration(\n                event_type=BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent,\n                condition=_upkeep_condition,\n                effect=_upkeep_effect,\n                source=source,\n                controller=controller,\n            )\n        )\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":83815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"869020ce-61a2-4539-a24f-e2f7c1962f45","request_id":"req_011Cbw6QgXh6YfWM85gGrhWB"}
