{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_017jg6zniGYWsHJ2bHZGQfr7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough to implement sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer). Let me check what existing API exists for surveil and the -1 / -2 abilities.\n\nFor **surveil**, I'll follow the Lightshell Duo pattern from fdn_157:\n- Look at top N cards of library\n- For each, ask yes/no to put in graveyard or keep\n- Cards kept on top stay in library order\n\nFor the **-1: Any number of target players each discard a card**:\n- I need to choose \"any number\" of players, then each discards\n- Using `choose` to select players (can be 0, 1, or more)\n- Since the ability targets \"any number\", I'll ask the controller to choose which players, then each discards\n\nFor **-2: Return target creature card with MV ≤ 3 from graveyard to battlefield**:\n- Choose a creature card from controller's graveyard with MV ≤ 3\n- Put it on the battlefield\n\nFor **-7: Flip five coins; target opponent skips X turns**:\n- Choose target opponent, flip 5 coins, count heads, then set the opponent to skip that many turns using a `turns_to_skip` attribute (the turn engine would enforce this)\n\nNow I need to understand how targeting works for loyalty abilities, particularly how the `-1` ability resolves its target through the planeswalker's resolution system.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1600,"cache_read_input_tokens":105149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1600},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"01b04021-0bdc-44b3-b07e-3aec0c5f84fe","request_id":"req_011Cbw6iB3uWyBwkKZMFZesU"}
