{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YKGofxFg6g2MyKnPVYNNbF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# TODO — Implement SOS cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257\n2\t\n3\tThis is a prepared execution plan. It tells you **what to build first**, gives\n4\t**rough guidance on how** (which existing engine seam to reuse, which FDN card\n5\tto mirror), and lists the **pitfalls** to avoid. It is a *guide, not a spec* —\n6\t`card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt` are the source of truth. When the real engine\n7\tdisagrees with a claim here, trust the engine and the spec, fix the code, and jot\n8\ta one-line note next to the item. See `CONTEXT.md` for the vocabulary used below.\n9\t\n10\tYou are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and\n11\tmechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make\n12\tchanges that don't break current behavior.\n13\t\n14\t## Prime directive\n15\t\n16\tOne mind builds all ten cards. The goal is **surgical, additive reuse**: build\n17\tor learn each shared seam once, then reuse it. The trap on cards like these is\n18\tbuilding a **separate general engine subsystem for each single-card mechanic** —\n19\tdo that six times and you get sprawling, speculative machinery where a handful of\n20\tsmall, focused edits would do, and that machinery tends to drift from what the\n21\tcards actually do. Keep changes small and local. Read `## Pitfalls` before you\n22\twrite any engine code.\n23\t\n24\t## The engine already supports most of this — reuse, don't rebuild\n25\t\n26\tRead the source for exact signatures and docstrings; do **not** trust any spec\n27\tdoc over the actual `engine/*.py`. These shared seams already exist and cover the\n28\tbulk of the ten cards:\n29\t\n30\t| Capability | Existing seam (read the source) | Mirror this FDN card | Reused by |\n31\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n32\t| Cost reduction (generic only) | `CardImpl.cost_reduction(self, game)` hook in `engine/card.py`; called by `get_cost_reduction` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_57 | sos_1, sos_245 |\n33\t| Cast without paying, from any zone | `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_194 (Etali), fdn_161 (Omniscience) | sos_1 (graveyard), sos_13 + sos_120 (exile) |\n34\t| Copy a spell on the stack | `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` in `engine/stack.py` (resolves via `on_resolve`, fires no cast event — copies are not \"cast\") | fdn_248 | sos_120, sos_226 |\n35\t| Colors / amount of mana spent | `card.colors_spent` set at cast time in `engine/casting.py` (~line 229); deterministic in tests via `mana_pool.pay(cost, choices=...)` | — | sos_4 (colors), sos_57 (amount) |\n36\t| Triggered abilities | `register_triggers(self, game)` hook + `TriggerRegistration` / `game.trigger_manager.register(...)` in `engine/triggers.py`; event classes in `engine/events.py` | fdn_235, fdn_81 | most cards |\n37\t| Replacement effects (zone redirect) | `register_replacement_effects(self, game)` hook + `ReplacementEffect`; set `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"` | fdn_244, fdn_137 | sos_1 (\"exile instead\") |\n38\t| Loyalty abilities | `Planeswalker` + `get_loyalty_abilities()` → `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; read targets from `self.chosen_targets` (the engine sets it from the activation's targets; mirror fdn_81 only for the loyalty scaffolding, not its `_resolve_target` reads) | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_97 |\n39\t| Mana abilities | `Land` + `get_mana_abilities()` → `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` | (grep fdn lands) | sos_257 |\n40\t| Counter target spell | card-local: mirror an FDN counterspell's local `_counter_spell` (pop from stack → graveyard) + `can_cast` guard + `zone=Zone.STACK` targeting | fdn_48 (Refute) | sos_57 |\n41\t| Tokens | `create_token(game, player, token)` in `engine/game.py` | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_13 |\n42\t| Reanimate (graveyard → battlefield) | `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB automatically) | — | sos_97 (−2) |\n43\t| Helpers | `engine/game.py`: `draw_card`, `discard`, `deal_damage`, `exile`, `sacrifice`, `add_counter`, `tap`/`untap` | — | many |\n44\t\n45\tBefore adding anything to `engine/`, confirm the seam above doesn't already do\n46\tthe job. The first question for every clause is **\"which FDN card and which\n47\texisting hook already does this?\"** — not \"what new system do I need?\".\n48\t\n49\t## Build these three shared engine changes FIRST (small, additive)\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"3feac855-653a-4b9c-9588-cfb6aedac27c","timestamp":"2026-06-11T07:47:25.516Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/TODO.md","content":"# TODO — Implement SOS cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257\n\nThis is a prepared execution plan. It tells you **what to build first**, gives\n**rough guidance on how** (which existing engine seam to reuse, which FDN card\nto mirror), and lists the **pitfalls** to avoid. It is a *guide, not a spec* —\n`card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt` are the source of truth. When the real engine\ndisagrees with a claim here, trust the engine and the spec, fix the code, and jot\na one-line note next to the item. See `CONTEXT.md` for the vocabulary used below.\n\nYou are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and\nmechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make\nchanges that don't break current behavior.\n\n## Prime directive\n\nOne mind builds all ten cards. The goal is **surgical, additive reuse**: build\nor learn each shared seam once, then reuse it. The trap on cards like these is\nbuilding a **separate general engine subsystem for each single-card mechanic** —\ndo that six times and you get sprawling, speculative machinery where a handful of\nsmall, focused edits would do, and that machinery tends to drift from what the\ncards actually do. Keep changes small and local. Read `## Pitfalls` before you\nwrite any engine code.\n\n## The engine already supports most of this — reuse, don't rebuild\n\nRead the source for exact signatures and docstrings; do **not** trust any spec\ndoc over the actual `engine/*.py`. These shared seams already exist and cover the\nbulk of the ten cards:\n\n| Capability | Existing seam (read the source) | Mirror this FDN card | Reused by |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cost reduction (generic only) | `CardImpl.cost_reduction(self, game)` hook in `engine/card.py`; called by `get_cost_reduction` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_57 | sos_1, sos_245 |\n| Cast without paying, from any zone | `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_194 (Etali), fdn_161 (Omniscience) | sos_1 (graveyard), sos_13 + sos_120 (exile) |\n| Copy a spell on the stack | `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` in `engine/stack.py` (resolves via `on_resolve`, fires no cast event — copies are not \"cast\") | fdn_248 | sos_120, sos_226 |\n| Colors / amount of mana spent | `card.colors_spent` set at cast time in `engine/casting.py` (~line 229); deterministic in tests via `mana_pool.pay(cost, choices=...)` | — | sos_4 (colors), sos_57 (amount) |\n| Triggered abilities | `register_triggers(self, game)` hook + `TriggerRegistration` / `game.trigger_manager.register(...)` in `engine/triggers.py`; event classes in `engine/events.py` | fdn_235, fdn_81 | most cards |\n| Replacement effects (zone redirect) | `register_replacement_effects(self, game)` hook + `ReplacementEffect`; set `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"` | fdn_244, fdn_137 | sos_1 (\"exile instead\") |\n| Loyalty abilities | `Planeswalker` + `get_loyalty_abilities()` → `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; read targets from `self.chosen_targets` (the engine sets it from the activation's targets; mirror fdn_81 only for the loyalty scaffolding, not its `_resolve_target` reads) | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_97 |\n| Mana abilities | `Land` + `get_mana_abilities()` → `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` | (grep fdn lands) | sos_257 |\n| Counter target spell | card-local: mirror an FDN counterspell's local `_counter_spell` (pop from stack → graveyard) + `can_cast` guard + `zone=Zone.STACK` targeting | fdn_48 (Refute) | sos_57 |\n| Tokens | `create_token(game, player, token)` in `engine/game.py` | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_13 |\n| Reanimate (graveyard → battlefield) | `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB automatically) | — | sos_97 (−2) |\n| Helpers | `engine/game.py`: `draw_card`, `discard`, `deal_damage`, `exile`, `sacrifice`, `add_counter`, `tap`/`untap` | — | many |\n\nBefore adding anything to `engine/`, confirm the seam above doesn't already do\nthe job. The first question for every clause is **\"which FDN card and which\nexisting hook already does this?\"** — not \"what new system do I need?\".\n\n## Build these three shared engine changes FIRST (small, additive)\n","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":300}}}
