{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111dqdBTBdvzCQghNRvKa4h","type":"tool_result","content":"50\t\n51\tEach is reused by more than one card. Build and verify them up front so the cards\n52\tthat depend on them just register ordinary triggers/hooks. Keep each tiny; run\n53\t`python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each.\n54\t\n55\t- **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`.** It is defined in `engine/events.py`\n56\t  (fields: `spell`, `card`, `controller`) but **never fired**. Fire it inside\n57\t  `cast_spell` (`engine/casting.py`) right after the spell is pushed to the stack,\n58\t  populating `spell=<the StackObject>`, `card`, and `controller`. Copies made by\n59\t  `copy_spell` do **not** go through `cast_spell`, so they correctly do not\n60\t  re-fire it. *Reused by:* sos_226 (Casualty), sos_257 (animated pump).\n61\t- **E2 — Add `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`.** No event fires at any\n62\t  main phase today. Add the event class to `engine/events.py` (model it on the\n63\t  fieldless `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`) and fire it from\n64\t  `GameState.advance_phase` (`engine/game_state.py`) — the single chokepoint every\n65\t  phase transition passes through — when the new phase becomes `PRECOMBAT_MAIN`,\n66\t  right **after** `empty_mana_pools()` so anything a handler adds to the pool\n67\t  survives into the main phase. Firing it here (not in `engine/turn.py`) makes it\n68\t  behave identically whether a turn is run normally or the state is advanced\n69\t  directly; a handler fired only from the turn loop would be skipped on a direct\n70\t  advance. Handlers identify \"your main phase\" by checking the active player.\n71\t  (Contrast E1, which belongs in `cast_spell` because casting always flows through\n72\t  that path.) *Reused by:* sos_57 (next main phase, once), sos_120 (each of your\n73\t  first main phases, recurring).\n74\t- **E3 — Aggregate cost reduction from the battlefield.** `get_cost_reduction`\n75\t  (`engine/casting.py`) only calls the spell's own `cost_reduction` hook. Extend\n76\t  it to also add reductions contributed by the caster's battlefield permanents:\n77\t  for each permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell) -> int`,\n78\t  add it when the spell being cast is an instant/sorcery. Clamp as today\n79\t  (generic-only, ≥ 0). *Reused by:* sos_245 (grants affinity to your spells); any\n80\t  future \"your spells cost less\" card. (sos_1 / sos_245 self-reduction still use\n81\t  the normal `cost_reduction` hook.)\n82\t\n83\t## Per-card gaps — keep them CARD-LOCAL\n84\t\n85\tThe remaining mechanics each serve **exactly one card**. Implement each as the\n86\tsmallest local change in that card's `card_impl.py` (plus the tiny additive\n87\tengine edit noted), and add a one-line comment on any deliberate limitation. Do\n88\t**not** generalize these into engine subsystems. Specifics live in the per-card\n89\titems below: Miracle (sos_201), the split/back-face (sos_13), the restricted-mana\n90\ttag + land animation (sos_257), and coin-flips / skip-turns / surveil (sos_97).\n91\t\n92\t**E1–E3 and the per-card edits below are not an exhaustive list of the engine\n93\tchanges you may make.** If a card genuinely needs an engine change that isn't\n94\tlisted — a new event, a field on a permanent or on game state, a small helper —\n95\tyou are free to add it. The bar is *minimal, additive, and justified by a real\n96\tcard need*, not a fixed whitelist; what to avoid is a speculative general\n97\t*subsystem* for one card's mechanic, not engine edits as such. Whenever you touch\n98\t`engine/`, keep the change as small as possible, comment any deliberate\n99\tlimitation, never rename/move/delete existing symbols, and keep `engine_tests/`\n100\tgreen.\n101\t\n102\t## Build order\n103\t\n104\tWork the items **in order, one at a time**. Items E1–E3 are the shared engine\n105\tchanges above; the card items follow in dependency order (shared seams first,\n106\tthen the cards that reuse them; simplest → hardest). For every card: read its\n107\t`card_spec.json`, enumerate each oracle clause and its edges, mirror the nearest\n108\tFDN card, reuse the named seam, write 2–5 real-engine tests through `test_utils`,\n109\tthen run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` before moving on.\n110\t\n111\t- [ ] **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell`** (see above). Verify\n112\t  with a probe trigger that casting an instant fires it once with the right\n113\t  `controller` and `spell`.\n114\t- [ ] **E2 — Add + fire `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`** from\n115\t  `GameState.advance_phase`, after `empty_mana_pools()` (see above). Verify a\n116\t  registered trigger fires — and any mana it adds persists — when the state is\n117\t  advanced directly to the active player's precombat main.\n118\t- [ ] **E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation in `get_cost_reduction`**\n119\t  (see above). Verify a permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction` reduces an\n120\t  instant's generic cost, clamped at 0.\n121\t\n122\t- [ ] **sos_4 — Together as One** *(warm-up: mana-spent, pure resolve)*\n123\t  - Clauses: Converge — X = number of colors of mana spent; target player draws\n124\t    X, deal X damage to any target, you gain X life.\n125\t  - Reuse: read `card.colors_spent` in `on_resolve`; `X = len(set(colors_spent))`.\n126\t    `draw_card`, `deal_damage`; set life directly. Targets via\n127\t    `get_targets`/`self.chosen_targets`.\n128\t  - Edges: X = 0 (colorless cast) → draws/deals/gains 0; \"any target\" is a player\n129\t    or creature. Tests set colors deterministically via `mana_pool.pay(choices=)`.\n130\t\n131\t- [ ] **sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic** *(cost reduction + free cast + trigger + replacement)*\n132\t  - Clauses: costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard; Reach; on\n133\t    attack, may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard for free (if only one\n134\t    legal target, auto-select it instead of prompting); if that spell would go to\n135\t    the graveyard, exile it instead.\n136\t  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook (count instant/sorcery in your graveyard);\n137\t    `Keyword` for Reach; `register_triggers` on `AttacksTriggeredEvent`;\n138\t    `cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`; for exile-instead,\n139\t    register a `ReplacementEffect` that sets the spell's\n140\t    `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"`.\n141\t  - Edges: empty graveyard (no reduction; \"may\" trigger with no legal target);\n142\t    reduction is generic-only and clamps at 0.\n143\t\n144\t- [x] **sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer** *(uses E3; affinity self + grant)*\n145\t  - Clauses: Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control);\n146\t    Flying, Deathtouch; your instant/sorcery spells also have affinity for creatures.\n147\t  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook for its OWN affinity (count creatures you\n148\t    control); `Keyword.FLYING | DEATHTOUCH`. For the grant, expose\n149\t    `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)` returning your creature count — E3"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecc45bba-5220-4378-9482-c0a0c3fff5e1","uuid":"b45d379e-6c6d-47a7-a470-08813b01e624","timestamp":"2026-06-11T07:47:28.227Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/TODO.md","content":"\nEach is reused by more than one card. Build and verify them up front so the cards\nthat depend on them just register ordinary triggers/hooks. Keep each tiny; run\n`python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each.\n\n- **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`.** It is defined in `engine/events.py`\n  (fields: `spell`, `card`, `controller`) but **never fired**. Fire it inside\n  `cast_spell` (`engine/casting.py`) right after the spell is pushed to the stack,\n  populating `spell=<the StackObject>`, `card`, and `controller`. Copies made by\n  `copy_spell` do **not** go through `cast_spell`, so they correctly do not\n  re-fire it. *Reused by:* sos_226 (Casualty), sos_257 (animated pump).\n- **E2 — Add `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`.** No event fires at any\n  main phase today. Add the event class to `engine/events.py` (model it on the\n  fieldless `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`) and fire it from\n  `GameState.advance_phase` (`engine/game_state.py`) — the single chokepoint every\n  phase transition passes through — when the new phase becomes `PRECOMBAT_MAIN`,\n  right **after** `empty_mana_pools()` so anything a handler adds to the pool\n  survives into the main phase. Firing it here (not in `engine/turn.py`) makes it\n  behave identically whether a turn is run normally or the state is advanced\n  directly; a handler fired only from the turn loop would be skipped on a direct\n  advance. Handlers identify \"your main phase\" by checking the active player.\n  (Contrast E1, which belongs in `cast_spell` because casting always flows through\n  that path.) *Reused by:* sos_57 (next main phase, once), sos_120 (each of your\n  first main phases, recurring).\n- **E3 — Aggregate cost reduction from the battlefield.** `get_cost_reduction`\n  (`engine/casting.py`) only calls the spell's own `cost_reduction` hook. Extend\n  it to also add reductions contributed by the caster's battlefield permanents:\n  for each permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell) -> int`,\n  add it when the spell being cast is an instant/sorcery. Clamp as today\n  (generic-only, ≥ 0). *Reused by:* sos_245 (grants affinity to your spells); any\n  future \"your spells cost less\" card. (sos_1 / sos_245 self-reduction still use\n  the normal `cost_reduction` hook.)\n\n## Per-card gaps — keep them CARD-LOCAL\n\nThe remaining mechanics each serve **exactly one card**. Implement each as the\nsmallest local change in that card's `card_impl.py` (plus the tiny additive\nengine edit noted), and add a one-line comment on any deliberate limitation. Do\n**not** generalize these into engine subsystems. Specifics live in the per-card\nitems below: Miracle (sos_201), the split/back-face (sos_13), the restricted-mana\ntag + land animation (sos_257), and coin-flips / skip-turns / surveil (sos_97).\n\n**E1–E3 and the per-card edits below are not an exhaustive list of the engine\nchanges you may make.** If a card genuinely needs an engine change that isn't\nlisted — a new event, a field on a permanent or on game state, a small helper —\nyou are free to add it. The bar is *minimal, additive, and justified by a real\ncard need*, not a fixed whitelist; what to avoid is a speculative general\n*subsystem* for one card's mechanic, not engine edits as such. Whenever you touch\n`engine/`, keep the change as small as possible, comment any deliberate\nlimitation, never rename/move/delete existing symbols, and keep `engine_tests/`\ngreen.\n\n## Build order\n\nWork the items **in order, one at a time**. Items E1–E3 are the shared engine\nchanges above; the card items follow in dependency order (shared seams first,\nthen the cards that reuse them; simplest → hardest). For every card: read its\n`card_spec.json`, enumerate each oracle clause and its edges, mirror the nearest\nFDN card, reuse the named seam, write 2–5 real-engine tests through `test_utils`,\nthen run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` before moving on.\n\n- [ ] **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell`** (see above). Verify\n  with a probe trigger that casting an instant fires it once with the right\n  `controller` and `spell`.\n- [ ] **E2 — Add + fire `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`** from\n  `GameState.advance_phase`, after `empty_mana_pools()` (see above). Verify a\n  registered trigger fires — and any mana it adds persists — when the state is\n  advanced directly to the active player's precombat main.\n- [ ] **E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation in `get_cost_reduction`**\n  (see above). Verify a permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction` reduces an\n  instant's generic cost, clamped at 0.\n\n- [ ] **sos_4 — Together as One** *(warm-up: mana-spent, pure resolve)*\n  - Clauses: Converge — X = number of colors of mana spent; target player draws\n    X, deal X damage to any target, you gain X life.\n  - Reuse: read `card.colors_spent` in `on_resolve`; `X = len(set(colors_spent))`.\n    `draw_card`, `deal_damage`; set life directly. Targets via\n    `get_targets`/`self.chosen_targets`.\n  - Edges: X = 0 (colorless cast) → draws/deals/gains 0; \"any target\" is a player\n    or creature. Tests set colors deterministically via `mana_pool.pay(choices=)`.\n\n- [ ] **sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic** *(cost reduction + free cast + trigger + replacement)*\n  - Clauses: costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard; Reach; on\n    attack, may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard for free (if only one\n    legal target, auto-select it instead of prompting); if that spell would go to\n    the graveyard, exile it instead.\n  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook (count instant/sorcery in your graveyard);\n    `Keyword` for Reach; `register_triggers` on `AttacksTriggeredEvent`;\n    `cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`; for exile-instead,\n    register a `ReplacementEffect` that sets the spell's\n    `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"`.\n  - Edges: empty graveyard (no reduction; \"may\" trigger with no legal target);\n    reduction is generic-only and clamps at 0.\n\n- [x] **sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer** *(uses E3; affinity self + grant)*\n  - Clauses: Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control);\n    Flying, Deathtouch; your instant/sorcery spells also have affinity for creatures.\n  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook for its OWN affinity (count creatures you\n    control); `Keyword.FLYING | DEATHTOUCH`. For the grant, expose\n    `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)` returning your creature count — E3","numLines":100,"startLine":50,"totalLines":300}}}
